{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788132865,"nonce":"2W8wM7gvPX3yuR7ptv137cZCY88=","message":"AMENDMENT from the action-surface audit — orchestrator, session 4.\n\n**1. `CanPlaceBlueprintAt` is NOT \"THE validator\", and the spec calls it that.**\n`RimWorld/GenConstruct.cs:231` performs no research check. The gate lives in\n`Designator_Build.Visible` (`RimWorld/Designator_Build.cs:125`,\n`!entDef.IsResearchFinished`, plus a `maxTechLevelToBuild` check just above).\nVerified by the orchestrator. Without reproducing it, `build` and `place-layout`\nwill cheerfully blueprint unresearched buildings — a god-hand that looks\ncorrect. This is the concrete instance of the new **DESIGN §Action model\nwidget-gate invariant**; read that entry before writing the verb, and cite the\nfile:line in a comment the way `Blockers.cs` does.\n\n**2. \"Roof areas\" is close to a no-op for this spec's own acceptance case.**\n`Verse/Room.cs:701` → `AutoBuildRoofAreaSetter.TryGenerateAreaNow`\n(`Verse/AutoBuildRoofAreaSetter.cs:42-61`): an enclosed player-faction room that\ndoes not touch the map edge, ≤26 regions, ≤320 cells, not a doorway, gets its\nBuildRoof area generated AUTOMATICALLY. The 5×7 bedroom in this spec's\nacceptance is 35 cells — it qualifies, so it will roof itself. The real need for\nroof designators is **un**roofing and rooms over 320 cells, neither of which the\nscope names. Adjust the acceptance so it demonstrates something the game was not\ngoing to do anyway.\n\n**3. `Install` / reinstall belongs here, not in 3.2.**\n`RimWorld/Designator_Install.cs:116` — moving a minified thing without\nrebuilding it. It is a placement operation and shares this spec's validation\npath.\n\n**4. Free layout primitives worth knowing about**, both one call:\n`Building_SunLamp` yields \"make matching growing zone\"\n(`RimWorld/Building_SunLamp.cs:20-28`) and `Building_OrbitalTradeBeacon` yields\n\"make beacon stockpile\" (`:24-32`). The layout IR does not have to compute those\nfootprints itself.\n\n**5. `place-layout` preflight** should report per-cell failures in the\n`removal`/`reason` shape `Blockers.cs` already ships (DESIGN decisions log,\n2026-08-30), so the agent can choose between \"clear this and retry\" and \"site it\nelsewhere\". That was always the intent; `Blockers.cs` now exists to be called.","files":null}]}